--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/fleet-device-pairing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Hermes Fleet device pairing (gateway side)
+
+A short-lived, single-use, origin-scoped pairing invitation that a Hermes Fleet phone
+exchanges for a revocable device credential. This is the server half; the phone half
+lives in the Hermes Fleet app repository (`docs/fleet-device-pairing.md` there has the
+user flow and the client-side checks).
+
+## Requirements
+
+- The dashboard auth gate is engaged (non-loopback bind or `dashboard.public_url`) and a
+  real sign-in provider is registered. Pairing endpoints answer `409 pairing_unavailable`
+  otherwise.
+- `dashboard.public_url` (or `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL`) is the gateway's **https**
+  origin on a real hostname, no path. Invitations are refused for `http`, IP literals,
+  `localhost`, single-label hosts, user-info and paths.
+- Optional profile settings in `config.yaml`: `dashboard.pairing_display_name` (name shown on the
+  phone) and `dashboard.pairing_app_ids` (list of `<TeamID>.<bundle id>` values) to serve the Apple
+  app-site-association document for Universal Links. An empty app-ID list disables that document.
+
+## Owner surface (signed-in, non-device session)
+
+| Method and path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `POST /api/fleet/pairing/invitations` `{label?, ttl_seconds?}` | Create an invitation (60 s - 15 min). Returns the link **once**. |
+| `GET /api/fleet/pairing/invitations` | Pending invitations (no secrets). |
+| `DELETE /api/fleet/pairing/invitations/{id}` | Cancel a pending invitation. |
+| `GET /api/fleet/devices` | Paired devices. |
+| `DELETE /api/fleet/devices/{id}` | Revoke a device; its sessions end on the next request. |
+
+The same operations are available on the host:
+`python -m hermes_cli.fleet_pairing_cli invite|invitations|cancel|devices|revoke`.
+
+## Phone surface (authenticated by a secret in the POST body)
+
+| Method and path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `POST /api/fleet/pairing/preview` `{invitation_id, secret}` | Gateway identity and requested access. **Does not consume.** |
+| `POST /api/fleet/pairing/redeem` `{invitation_id, secret, device_name}` | Consumes the invitation atomically; returns the device credential once. |
+| `POST /auth/device-login` `{device_credential}` | Exchange the credential for a short-lived session cookie. |
+| `POST /auth/device-revoke` `{device_credential}` | The device revokes itself. |
+| `GET /pair`, `GET /.well-known/apple-app-site-association` | Secret-free landing page; Universal Links association (only when configured). |
+
+## Security properties
+
+- 128-bit invitation id, 256-bit secret in the URL fragment; only SHA-256 digests stored.
+- Redemption is a single `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction with a compare-and-set
+  (`UPDATE ... WHERE state='pending' AND expires_at > now`), so concurrent redemptions
+  (threads or processes) have one winner.
+- A secret presented to a different `Host` than the invitation's origin is "invalid" and
+  does not consume it. The state of an invitation is revealed only to a caller who proves
+  the secret; five wrong secrets lock it.
+- Device sessions are served by a hidden `fleet-device` provider (not offered on the login
+  page or in `/api/auth/providers`). A device cannot create invitations or manage devices.
+- Secrets, links, credentials and session tokens are never logged; the audit log keeps
+  eight-character identifier prefixes and outcomes.
+
+## Tests
+
+`tests/hermes_cli/test_fleet_device_pairing_store.py` (security properties),
+`..._http.py` (gated app end to end), `..._network.py` (real uvicorn + TLS, 16 concurrent
+redemptions, WebSocket ticket), `test_fleet_pairing_cli.py`. They are `unittest` cases and
+also run under pytest. `scripts/fleet_pairing_dev_server.py` boots the real app on
+loopback with a throwaway home and certificate for client-side end-to-end tests.
